package sqlite:wasm-stub@0.1.0;

/// Declining provider for every function-carrying `sqlite:wasm/*`
/// surface sqlite-lib imports but standalone-composed consumers
/// (cache.wasm, sqlitewasm.wasm) never actually invoke at runtime.
/// Composed via `wac plug` AFTER sqlite-lib.wasm so its
/// function-carrying imports resolve at instantiation time.
///
/// Interfaces exported here:
///
///   * `sqlite:wasm/extension-loader@0.1.0`
///       three methods, all return `loader-error`. Cache/sqlitewasm
///       don't dynamic-load extensions.
///
///   * `sqlite:wasm/dispatch@0.1.0`
///       34 methods routing scalar / aggregate / vtab / hook calls
///       into a runtime extension registry. Standalone consumers have
///       no registry — every `result<T, string>` returns
///       `Err("...")` and the non-`result` returns pick the most
///       declining default (`vtab-eof` = true so cursors terminate,
///       `authorize` = deny to fail-closed, hooks are no-ops, etc.).
///
///   * `sqlite:wasm/opfs-host@0.1.0`
///       8 methods backing the browser's OPFS-backed VFS. Native /
///       standalone wasm runtimes reach the filesystem via wasi:fs,
///       not through opfs-host, so every method returns
///       `opfs-error{code=io, message="not supported in standalone"}`.
///
/// Not exported here — kept as unresolved type-only imports on the
/// composed artifact, honored by wasmtime's component-model
/// linker without a host provider:
///
///   * `sqlite:extension/{types,http,policy,metadata,vtab}@1.0.0`
///       sqlite-lib imports these purely as TYPE declarations
///       (`variant method` for http, records for the rest) with no
///       function members. `wac plug` matches sockets and plugs by
///       function signature — a type-only interface can't be
///       plug-provided, only imported at instantiation. This mirrors
///       the shape already shipped in artifacts/extensions/
///       sqlitewasm.wasm at @0.1.0, which the ducklink host has
///       loaded without a native provider since Bug 4b.
///
/// All stubs are decline-everything — no state, no side effects. If
/// a runtime consumer actually calls one of these methods it will
/// receive a clearly-worded error rather than a wrong answer.
world sqlite-loader-stub {
    export sqlite:wasm/extension-loader@0.1.0;
    export sqlite:wasm/dispatch@0.1.0;
    export sqlite:wasm/opfs-host@0.1.0;
}
